(5255233, 763659, 95940, '<td valign="top">I am afraid i am giving you a 1. This is a good shot of a spider, but this does not qualify as a pet portrait. Had this been a Macro challenge, or insect challenge i would consider a 6 or 7. It is vibrant and the focus is nice, but it seems just a bit noisy, and there are a few blown out spots on it.</td>', 'I am afraid i am giving you a 1. This is a good shot of a spider, but this does not qualify as a pet portrait. Had this been a Macro challenge, or insect challenge i would consider a 6 or 7. It is vibrant and the focus is nice, but it seems just a bit noisy, and there are a few blown out spots on it.', '2009-02-13 16:27:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5255235, 763642, 95940, '<td valign="top">I gave a 1 because i doubt that this is a pet of yours, or of anyones. Mother natures pet doesn''t qualify for me. Nice Crop, clean, vibrant, and sharp, but wrong challenge.</td>', 'I gave a 1 because i doubt that this is a pet of yours, or of anyones. Mother natures pet doesn''t qualify for me. Nice Crop, clean, vibrant, and sharp, but wrong challenge.', '2009-02-13 16:28:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5255305, 763387, 65234, '<td valign="top">Unusual choise of subject for this, and given your title you apparently weren''t trying to meet the challenge with him.  Color is unnatural and somehow even the teeth are orange (maybe a hue shift); shot is in need of some sharpening, but then I suspect you were not trying to win a ribbon with this one so perhaps these were all artistic choices.</td>', 'Unusual choise of subject for this, and given your title you apparently weren''t trying to meet the challenge with him.  Color is unnatural and somehow even the teeth are orange (maybe a hue shift); shot is in need of some sharpening, but then I suspect you were not trying to win a ribbon with this one so perhaps these were all artistic choices.', '2009-02-13 17:49:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5255306, 764338, 65234, '<td valign="top">A low perspective can be interesting in a pet portrait, but in general too close a view of nostrils is not visually pleasing to many people.  Lighting is exceptionally bright and not flattering.  On the plus side, it looks like maybe the dog was getting a chest rub, so at least the portrait session wasn''t stressful for the model.</td>', 'A low perspective can be interesting in a pet portrait, but in general too close a view of nostrils is not visually pleasing to many people.  Lighting is exceptionally bright and not flattering.  On the plus side, it looks like maybe the dog was getting a chest rub, so at least the portrait session wasn''t stressful for the model.', '2009-02-13 17:52:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5255310, 764547, 65234, '<td valign="top">A toy doesn''t quite qualify as a pet in my mind, and the very bright light is fairly overwhelming to the panda.</td>', 'A toy doesn''t quite qualify as a pet in my mind, and the very bright light is fairly overwhelming to the panda.', '2009-02-13 17:54:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5255313, 764476, 65234, '<td valign="top">Lovely cat (medium-haired black cats are a favorite of mine) but there are some things I would do differently.  A sheet or blanket behind the cat would create a nice, non-distracting backdrop, and bouncing the flash off the ceiling might eliminate the glowing green pupils.</td>', 'Lovely cat (medium-haired black cats are a favorite of mine) but there are some things I would do differently.  A sheet or blanket behind the cat would create a nice, non-distracting backdrop, and bouncing the flash off the ceiling might eliminate the glowing green pupils.', '2009-02-13 17:56:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5255316, 764485, 65234, '<td valign="top">Dog is adorable and the carpet is a good background.  The tennis ball makes a nice prop.  Shot could be a little sharper on the face.  Big issue here is the glowing green pupils; options are to take the shot with a flash bounced off the ceiling instead of pointed at the dog, or in PP either try desaturating and darkening greens or shifting them to brown and darkening.</td>', 'Dog is adorable and the carpet is a good background.  The tennis ball makes a nice prop.  Shot could be a little sharper on the face.  Big issue here is the glowing green pupils; options are to take the shot with a flash bounced off the ceiling instead of pointed at the dog, or in PP either try desaturating and darkening greens or shifting them to brown and darkening.', '2009-02-13 18:00:14.000000', NULL, 1),
