(5258951, 763983, 11467, '<td valign="top">The lighting is not too bad in this.<br/>It could be made more interesting by moving it a bit more to the side. The catchlight in the middle of the left eye gives the impression of on camera flash. ;)<br/>Focus is spot on and iuse of DOF to concentrate the focus on the face-eyes works. Also the image seems to be portraying the personality of a pet quite well. Lazy dog ;)<br/>I''m not sure that the crop works as well as it could. I don''t like the legs being chopped off like that.<br/>Also a because the dog is laying in his (her) er its bed like that gives the impression of a snap shot compared to some of the setup photos in this challenge where you can see that an effort has been made to make a professional looking portrait.</td>', 'The lighting is not too bad in this.It could be made more interesting by moving it a bit more to the side. The catchlight in the middle of the left eye gives the impression of on camera flash. ;)Focus is spot on and iuse of DOF to concentrate the focus on the face-eyes works. Also the image seems to be portraying the personality of a pet quite well. Lazy dog ;)I''m not sure that the crop works as well as it could. I don''t like the legs being chopped off like that.Also a because the dog is laying in his (her) er its bed like that gives the impression of a snap shot compared to some of the setup photos in this challenge where you can see that an effort has been made to make a professional looking portrait.', '2009-02-16 11:02:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258968, 764614, 100773, '<td valign="top">Those dogs always tilts their head like that! Why do they have to be so darn cute! Very well shot too!</td>', 'Those dogs always tilts their head like that! Why do they have to be so darn cute! Very well shot too!', '2009-02-16 11:32:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258970, 764589, 100773, '<td valign="top">I think my dog thought the same thing when I suddenly looked directly into the flash... He can still see though. I would try to put a thin, white paper in front of the flash or tone it down a few steps; it looks a bit harsh to me.</td>', 'I think my dog thought the same thing when I suddenly looked directly into the flash... He can still see though. I would try to put a thin, white paper in front of the flash or tone it down a few steps; it looks a bit harsh to me.', '2009-02-16 11:34:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258973, 764592, 100773, '<td valign="top">HAHAHA!!!! It looks like your cat is bored out of his mind! What an unique pose! To bad this was basic editing, because the colors could''ve been a bit stronger. But that pose right there... Perfect title! This made my day!</td>', 'HAHAHA!!!! It looks like your cat is bored out of his mind! What an unique pose! To bad this was basic editing, because the colors could''ve been a bit stronger. But that pose right there... Perfect title! This made my day!', '2009-02-16 11:38:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258974, 764075, 11467, '<td valign="top">The catch light in the middle of the eye here gives the impression of on camera flash. On a second appraisal I can see that it isn''t as the light is a little softer, however appears to still be coming from pretty close to the camera.<br/>I would try moving the light a little more to the left and if you have a reflector either use this to fill the shadows, or try to reflect some light back onto the top of the head. This will help create more separation of the dark fur against the dark background as they seem to be blending together a little.<br/>Black backgrounds are very difficult as they tend to create a vacuum of nothingness, and dark objects against a black background tend to blend in. You are almost better with a white background, which when unlighted will become grey, or a plain coloured background.<br/>I think what also doesn''t help this image is the blanket, which gives the impression of a snapshot when the dog was in its basket or bed. As this challenge is defined as Pet Portrait, then in my opinion a more studio like (Interpreted as sterile) background would probably be more fitting.</td>', 'The catch light in the middle of the eye here gives the impression of on camera flash. On a second appraisal I can see that it isn''t as the light is a little softer, however appears to still be coming from pretty close to the camera.I would try moving the light a little more to the left and if you have a reflector either use this to fill the shadows, or try to reflect some light back onto the top of the head. This will help create more separation of the dark fur against the dark background as they seem to be blending together a little.Black backgrounds are very difficult as they tend to create a vacuum of nothingness, and dark objects against a black background tend to blend in. You are almost better with a white background, which when unlighted will become grey, or a plain coloured background.I think what also doesn''t help this image is the blanket, which gives the impression of a snapshot when the dog was in its basket or bed. As this challenge is defined as Pet Portrait, then in my opinion a more studio like (Interpreted as sterile) background would probably be more fitting.', '2009-02-16 11:39:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258975, 764599, 100773, '<td valign="top">I love where you have placed the cat in this photo, but I would like to see the entire head.</td>', 'I love where you have placed the cat in this photo, but I would like to see the entire head.', '2009-02-16 11:39:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258977, 764629, 100773, '<td valign="top">Cat has a "oh, uhm... I was...ehm... I better go..." Beautifull!</td>', 'Cat has a "oh, uhm... I was...ehm... I better go..." Beautifull!', '2009-02-16 11:40:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258981, 764481, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice crop and great detail.</td>', 'Nice crop and great detail.', '2009-02-16 11:42:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258983, 764508, 23484, '<td valign="top">Wonderful composition and nice background.</td>', 'Wonderful composition and nice background.', '2009-02-16 11:43:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5258986, 764266, 100773, '<td valign="top">Elegant! Love your use of black and white. 8</td>', 'Elegant! Love your use of black and white. 8', '2009-02-16 11:43:29.000000', NULL, 1),
