(5259844, 763918, 50695, '<td valign="top">operatic and yet intensely personal. this photo is an aria of suffering.</td>', 'operatic and yet intensely personal. this photo is an aria of suffering.', '2009-02-16 23:33:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259963, 763898, 11467, '<td valign="top">Not really a portrait.<br/>Here is the wikipedia definition:<br/>A portrait is a painting, photograph, sculpture, or other artistic representation of a person, in which the face and its expression is predominant. The intent is to display the likeness, personality, and even the mood of the person. For this reason, in photography a portrait is generally not a snapshot, but a composed image of a person in a still position. A portrait often shows a person looking directly at the painter or photographer, in order to most successfully engage the subject with the viewer.<br/> <br/>I like the picture composition in that the dog in nicely placed in the intersection of the 1/3 lines in the bottom right of the picture, however the cropping of the hunter turns this photo into a snapshot.<br/>The end of the toes are cropped off, the gun is cropped, and the flourescent colour of the vest draws your attention from the actual subject.<br/>If the hunter was in say green, and in the background rather than the foreground then I think this picture could have done better.</td>', 'Not really a portrait.Here is the wikipedia definition:A portrait is a painting, photograph, sculpture, or other artistic representation of a person, in which the face and its expression is predominant. The intent is to display the likeness, personality, and even the mood of the person. For this reason, in photography a portrait is generally not a snapshot, but a composed image of a person in a still position. A portrait often shows a person looking directly at the painter or photographer, in order to most successfully engage the subject with the viewer. I like the picture composition in that the dog in nicely placed in the intersection of the 1/3 lines in the bottom right of the picture, however the cropping of the hunter turns this photo into a snapshot.The end of the toes are cropped off, the gun is cropped, and the flourescent colour of the vest draws your attention from the actual subject.If the hunter was in say green, and in the background rather than the foreground then I think this picture could have done better.', '2009-02-17 01:23:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259968, 763370, 11467, '<td valign="top">This is not really a portrait.<br/>I think the subject is just a part of the overal image rather than dominating it.<br/>Here is the wikipedia definition:<br/>A portrait is a painting, photograph, sculpture, or other artistic representation of a person, in which the face and its expression is predominant. The intent is to display the likeness, personality, and even the mood of the person. For this reason, in photography a portrait is generally not a snapshot, but a composed image of a person in a still position. A portrait often shows a person looking directly at the painter or photographer, in order to most successfully engage the subject with the viewer.</td>', 'This is not really a portrait.I think the subject is just a part of the overal image rather than dominating it.Here is the wikipedia definition:A portrait is a painting, photograph, sculpture, or other artistic representation of a person, in which the face and its expression is predominant. The intent is to display the likeness, personality, and even the mood of the person. For this reason, in photography a portrait is generally not a snapshot, but a composed image of a person in a still position. A portrait often shows a person looking directly at the painter or photographer, in order to most successfully engage the subject with the viewer.', '2009-02-17 01:26:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259978, 763699, 11467, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, it is a portrait, and the lighting doesn''t look to bad, howwever the closeup wideangle nature of the photo is not exactly creating an attractive photo of your loved one.<br/>A little more attention to the background and cropping would have helped your score too.</td>', 'Hmmm, it is a portrait, and the lighting doesn''t look to bad, howwever the closeup wideangle nature of the photo is not exactly creating an attractive photo of your loved one.A little more attention to the background and cropping would have helped your score too.', '2009-02-17 01:37:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259983, 763365, 11467, '<td valign="top">On camera flash doesn''t help this image.<br/>Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.<br/> <br/>The background is a bit busy detracting from the face.<br/>Your white balance is a little off. Either set this in the camera to flash (When using the flash) or adjust it in a photo editing program afterwards to get rid of that blue tint.<br/>I would increase the exposure a little and add a little more contrast and you could make quite a nice photo out of this</td>', 'On camera flash doesn''t help this image.Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer. The background is a bit busy detracting from the face.Your white balance is a little off. Either set this in the camera to flash (When using the flash) or adjust it in a photo editing program afterwards to get rid of that blue tint.I would increase the exposure a little and add a little more contrast and you could make quite a nice photo out of this', '2009-02-17 01:40:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259984, 764469, 11467, '<td valign="top">This is a little too close for an attractive portrait. Also a little attention to the background could have helped this (A little). the bright colours against the brown dog draw my attention completely away from the subject.</td>', 'This is a little too close for an attractive portrait. Also a little attention to the background could have helped this (A little). the bright colours against the brown dog draw my attention completely away from the subject.', '2009-02-17 01:42:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259992, 764534, 11467, '<td valign="top">On camera flash doesn''t help this image.<br/>Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.<br/>I can see you have gone to some effort to create a nice photo here and respect your effort to setup a plain background. I think Black is not a good colour as it creates a vacume that draws attention more than it should. Better is a plain colour or grey.<br/>Crop is good and I like that you have gotr down to eye level with your pet to take the photo.</td>', 'On camera flash doesn''t help this image.Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.I can see you have gone to some effort to create a nice photo here and respect your effort to setup a plain background. I think Black is not a good colour as it creates a vacume that draws attention more than it should. Better is a plain colour or grey.Crop is good and I like that you have gotr down to eye level with your pet to take the photo.', '2009-02-17 01:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259993, 763819, 11467, '<td valign="top">This is difficult to judge.<br/>Do I say overexposed snapshot, or WOW a beautiful highkey portrait. Unfortunately my tendency is towards the first as the background is not uniform and distracts a little, and on my monitor (Manually calibrated) the neck and lower jaw blend into the background.. I would also have preferred a crop to have maybe included the ears.<br/>Nice looking dog by the way.</td>', 'This is difficult to judge.Do I say overexposed snapshot, or WOW a beautiful highkey portrait. Unfortunately my tendency is towards the first as the background is not uniform and distracts a little, and on my monitor (Manually calibrated) the neck and lower jaw blend into the background.. I would also have preferred a crop to have maybe included the ears.Nice looking dog by the way.', '2009-02-17 01:56:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259995, 764349, 11467, '<td valign="top">Sorry but this comes across as a snapshot.<br/>The backgrounsd doesn''t help the image, the shadows on the face and slightly out of focus also don''t help. Wide angle should not be used close up in a portrait, and standing above and looking down on the dog also help portray a snapshot. Get down to eye level with your dog.</td>', 'Sorry but this comes across as a snapshot.The backgrounsd doesn''t help the image, the shadows on the face and slightly out of focus also don''t help. Wide angle should not be used close up in a portrait, and standing above and looking down on the dog also help portray a snapshot. Get down to eye level with your dog.', '2009-02-17 02:00:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259996, 762788, 11467, '<td valign="top">Wide angle is not good for a portrait. All you can see is nose.<br/>The backgroud doesn''t help the image and the flair hides one of the eyes. Focus doesn''t seem to be on the eyes either.<br/>However you get an extra point for getting down to the same level as your pet.</td>', 'Wide angle is not good for a portrait. All you can see is nose.The backgroud doesn''t help the image and the flair hides one of the eyes. Focus doesn''t seem to be on the eyes either.However you get an extra point for getting down to the same level as your pet.', '2009-02-17 02:03:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259997, 763248, 11467, '<td valign="top">On camera flash doesn''t help this image.<br/>Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.</td>', 'On camera flash doesn''t help this image.Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.', '2009-02-17 02:03:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259998, 764181, 11467, '<td valign="top">On camera flash doesn''t help this image.<br/>Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.</td>', 'On camera flash doesn''t help this image.Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.', '2009-02-17 02:03:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5259999, 763834, 11467, '<td valign="top">Nice looking dog but not a photo that will do well here I think.<br/>The crop is a little tight.<br/>Lighting is uneven, bright at the back and so dark at the end of the nose, I can''t see any details theer. the bit of carpet also doesn''t help the image.</td>', 'Nice looking dog but not a photo that will do well here I think.The crop is a little tight.Lighting is uneven, bright at the back and so dark at the end of the nose, I can''t see any details theer. the bit of carpet also doesn''t help the image.', '2009-02-17 02:06:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260000, 763700, 11467, '<td valign="top">Man they look like they are having fun... Wouldn''t want to get in their way.<br/> <br/>Probably not doing so well as it is not really a portrait.<br/>Here is the wikipedia definition of a portrait:<br/>A portrait is a painting, photograph, sculpture, or other artistic representation of a person, in which the face and its expression is predominant. The intent is to display the likeness, personality, and even the mood of the person. For this reason, in photography a portrait is generally not a snapshot, but a composed image of a person in a still position. A portrait often shows a person looking directly at the painter or photographer, in order to most successfully engage the subject with the viewer.</td>', 'Man they look like they are having fun... Wouldn''t want to get in their way. Probably not doing so well as it is not really a portrait.Here is the wikipedia definition of a portrait:A portrait is a painting, photograph, sculpture, or other artistic representation of a person, in which the face and its expression is predominant. The intent is to display the likeness, personality, and even the mood of the person. For this reason, in photography a portrait is generally not a snapshot, but a composed image of a person in a still position. A portrait often shows a person looking directly at the painter or photographer, in order to most successfully engage the subject with the viewer.', '2009-02-17 02:06:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260002, 764353, 11467, '<td valign="top">Cute looking cat.<br/>A little more attention to the background i.e. remove the clutter would have helped, and maybe a portrait crop. The square crop is interesting, however as your background is messy it detracts rather than adds to the image.<br/>Even though I suspect you have used on camera flash, the light coming from the back left of the photo enhances the outline. Getting down to eye level is also good.</td>', 'Cute looking cat.A little more attention to the background i.e. remove the clutter would have helped, and maybe a portrait crop. The square crop is interesting, however as your background is messy it detracts rather than adds to the image.Even though I suspect you have used on camera flash, the light coming from the back left of the photo enhances the outline. Getting down to eye level is also good.', '2009-02-17 02:10:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260004, 764483, 11467, '<td valign="top">On camera flash doesn''t help this image.<br/>Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.<br/>Focus is also on the nose here rather than the eyes.</td>', 'On camera flash doesn''t help this image.Try to ues a more imaginitive lighting setup. Either try to get your flash off your camera, or use window lighting or a reflector to make things more interesting and softer.Focus is also on the nose here rather than the eyes.', '2009-02-17 02:10:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260006, 763722, 11467, '<td valign="top">I find this difficule to judge.<br/>Possible y little dark.<br/>The texture of the carped definitley distracts, however I like the interesting viewpoint. Focus appears to be good and sharp on the eyes. Maybe a reflector or very very low powered flash would help to ass a little bit of a glint to the eyes.</td>', 'I find this difficule to judge.Possible y little dark.The texture of the carped definitley distracts, however I like the interesting viewpoint. Focus appears to be good and sharp on the eyes. Maybe a reflector or very very low powered flash would help to ass a little bit of a glint to the eyes.', '2009-02-17 02:12:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260009, 763541, 11467, '<td valign="top">What an amazing looking cat and amazing eyes.<br/>Big minus points here for not removing that cussion on the left... the details count.<br/>However good crop and nice angle.</td>', 'What an amazing looking cat and amazing eyes.Big minus points here for not removing that cussion on the left... the details count.However good crop and nice angle.', '2009-02-17 02:14:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260010, 763829, 11467, '<td valign="top">I''m going to bump this up a bit, I like how the reflection is looking at me.<br/>Lighting and focus seem pretty good, and the B&amp;W works too.</td>', 'I''m going to bump this up a bit, I like how the reflection is looking at me.Lighting and focus seem pretty good, and the B&W works too.', '2009-02-17 02:15:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260011, 764640, 11467, '<td valign="top">The arm and the crop are what break this photo. Lighting seems nich and soft. That said, for anmals you are normally better without such a soft light source. If you are using a softbox (Which I think you are here) you are better off without the diffuser and just the silver inner lining of the box as this creates more shine in the fur. When the light is very doft, the fur becomes very matt.</td>', 'The arm and the crop are what break this photo. Lighting seems nich and soft. That said, for anmals you are normally better without such a soft light source. If you are using a softbox (Which I think you are here) you are better off without the diffuser and just the silver inner lining of the box as this creates more shine in the fur. When the light is very doft, the fur becomes very matt.', '2009-02-17 02:18:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260013, 764161, 11467, '<td valign="top">Well.. it is a snake and green, but for a portrait you need the head and in particular the eyes. If the head was in this photo it would have done lots better. Crop focus lighting are all ok.</td>', 'Well.. it is a snake and green, but for a portrait you need the head and in particular the eyes. If the head was in this photo it would have done lots better. Crop focus lighting are all ok.', '2009-02-17 02:20:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260014, 763826, 11467, '<td valign="top">Cute dog, but not a good portrait.<br/>Cropping just the tail out wasn''t good. <br/>The b&amp;w conversion is good, but the coloured frame really draws your attention away from the dog to the frame.<br/>Exposure is food, and nice that you have got down to the eye level of the dog.</td>', 'Cute dog, but not a good portrait.Cropping just the tail out wasn''t good. The b&w conversion is good, but the coloured frame really draws your attention away from the dog to the frame.Exposure is food, and nice that you have got down to the eye level of the dog.', '2009-02-17 02:22:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260015, 763113, 11467, '<td valign="top">Great picture, but doesn''t realy pass as a portrait.<br/>It could have done better if the face and eyes where visible, but on my monitor I only see a black outline with a tongue on snow.</td>', 'Great picture, but doesn''t realy pass as a portrait.It could have done better if the face and eyes where visible, but on my monitor I only see a black outline with a tongue on snow.', '2009-02-17 02:23:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260034, 763790, 60460, '<td valign="top">Obedient cat! so cute.</td>', 'Obedient cat! so cute.', '2009-02-17 03:52:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5260040, 763844, 11467, '<td valign="top">WHat a beautiful loking cat.<br/>I adore the yellow eyes .<br/>The uniform greyness of the image gives the impression of a selective desaturation<br/>The back lighting coming from over the shoulder creates a great outline around the head.<br/>Only negative thing I could say would be that the bunched up blanket doesn''t really suit a portrait image so well.<br/>Nice angle in that you have got down to the cats level, and the crop works well.<br/>Focus looks good and sharp on the eyes.</td>', 'WHat a beautiful loking cat.I adore the yellow eyes .The uniform greyness of the image gives the impression of a selective desaturationThe back lighting coming from over the shoulder creates a great outline around the head.Only negative thing I could say would be that the bunched up blanket doesn''t really suit a portrait image so well.Nice angle in that you have got down to the cats level, and the crop works well.Focus looks good and sharp on the eyes.', '2009-02-17 04:48:15.000000', NULL, 1),
