(5263842, 764387, 9602, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments. I knew the lighting was bad, but worked with what I had, and I was really going for the paw print thing more than lighting. The eyes I think are the most distracting part, but I couldn''t spot edit the shine out and don''t have an off-camera flash. Ah well, next time.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. I knew the lighting was bad, but worked with what I had, and I was really going for the paw print thing more than lighting. The eyes I think are the most distracting part, but I couldn''t spot edit the shine out and don''t have an off-camera flash. Ah well, next time.', '2009-02-18 18:08:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263844, 762922, 4793, '<td valign="top">Did you velcro this beauty into the glass, seriously a very nice shot.</td>', 'Did you velcro this beauty into the glass, seriously a very nice shot.', '2009-02-18 18:09:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263850, 764021, 52992, '<td valign="top">Sadly, this was originally tried with natural light - but there was not enough of it, so I had to use the flash.  I didn''t think to use my add-on flash though, which apparently shows and hurt the score.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Sadly, this was originally tried with natural light - but there was not enough of it, so I had to use the flash.  I didn''t think to use my add-on flash though, which apparently shows and hurt the score. ', '2009-02-18 18:12:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263864, 764528, 63218, '<td valign="top">I had to smile when I read your comments re the ''cropped ear,'' for I like what it does to the negative space, too, &amp; also the effect it has on the edge of the comp. Nobody said anything about the cropped whiskers, but I like that, too. The framing adds to the immediacy of the shot &amp; complements the alert, serious face. The catchlights in the eyes give a slightly sleepy twist to the expression.  IMO all cats are philosophers--I feel much more philosophical whenever I look at a cat!</td>', 'I had to smile when I read your comments re the ''cropped ear,'' for I like what it does to the negative space, too, & also the effect it has on the edge of the comp. Nobody said anything about the cropped whiskers, but I like that, too. The framing adds to the immediacy of the shot & complements the alert, serious face. The catchlights in the eyes give a slightly sleepy twist to the expression.  IMO all cats are philosophers--I feel much more philosophical whenever I look at a cat!', '2009-02-18 18:24:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263868, 763420, 63218, '<td valign="top">this is perfectly priceless just the way it is</td>', 'this is perfectly priceless just the way it is', '2009-02-18 18:28:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263895, 764528, 32997, '<td valign="top">oh man gotta kick the crop outta some people...:)</td>', 'oh man gotta kick the crop outta some people...:)', '2009-02-18 18:48:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263901, 763225, 32997, '<td valign="top">sorry I am no good to you if you care about your score, I didn''t vote...this shot is my favourite in this challenge, there is something very compelling about the tilted head, the shadows and yes of course the background...nice work!</td>', 'sorry I am no good to you if you care about your score, I didn''t vote...this shot is my favourite in this challenge, there is something very compelling about the tilted head, the shadows and yes of course the background...nice work!', '2009-02-18 18:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
