(5263997, 762922, 27133, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by VitaminB:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe:</b></div><hr/><i> hope we see you win many more times; will be fun to see if your attitude ends up in the win column as well.  best of luck. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Why some people feel compelled to chase some of DPC''s most dedicated, cooperative, and hard working members away from these contests is beyond me. <br/> <br/>I think all of us are frustrated by very low votes, and would like to understand them better. Judi, you have as much right to express your frustration, as they do in voting low to begin with. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thankyou for this.  I am not saying that I shouldn''t get low votes....because I believe I should get low votes.  But to get low votes indicates there is an error in my skills.  And I need to know where those errors are so I can improve.  Just like any person on here.  But how can that happen if the voters do not tell me where those errors are?</td>', 'Originally posted by VitaminB: Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe: hope we see you win many more times; will be fun to see if your attitude ends up in the win column as well.  best of luck.   Why some people feel compelled to chase some of DPC''s most dedicated, cooperative, and hard working members away from these contests is beyond me.  I think all of us are frustrated by very low votes, and would like to understand them better. Judi, you have as much right to express your frustration, as they do in voting low to begin with.   Thankyou for this.  I am not saying that I shouldn''t get low votes....because I believe I should get low votes.  But to get low votes indicates there is an error in my skills.  And I need to know where those errors are so I can improve.  Just like any person on here.  But how can that happen if the voters do not tell me where those errors are?', '2009-02-18 20:01:22.000000', NULL, 0),
